libkrun: the 3D virtio GPU of a Windows guest (viogpu3d): virgl and Neptune contexts beside Venus.
- Flags for virglrenderer's GL renderer on EGL/GLES (ANGLE on macOS), Neptune (capset 7, Direct3D)
  and native scanout textures; rutabaga is told about Neptune (patched rutabaga_gfx).
- vrend fences retire only when the renderer is polled (no fence thread on macOS): the worker polls
  every millisecond while the guest waits for a fence.
- A device reset frees what the guest made (scanouts, blobs mapped into its window, resources,
  contexts, pending fences) and the worker waits for the next activation: the renderer starts once
  per process. Windows resets the GPU on every driver restart and power-down and waits for it.
- Display events (VIRTIO_GPU_EVENT_DISPLAY, events_read/events_clear): while the guest shows a
  scanout at another size than the display's, one every few seconds, so it takes the display's size
  (viogpu3d boots at 1280x1024 and applies the host's size only on that event).

